#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1300 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "First Check branch (longer_than 2), rewritten for the wave-15 `dataset_domain` migration. ⚠⚠ The pre-migration shape of this scenario (row 1 `LB`, row 2 `LBX`, `#expectViolationAt row=2`) NO LONGER DETECTS ANYTHING: `dataset_domain` is `OperationExecutor.unsplitNameFromData`, which reads the ROW-0 `DOMAIN` cell verbatim and never looks at rows 2..N. That row-2..N loss is the accepted cost of Fix #172 / EC-67, so the malformed value now has to sit on row 0. Here every row carries a three-character `LBX`, so `longer_than 2` fires; `Sensitivity: Dataset` collapses it to one dataset-level finding. ⚠ The anchor row is deliberately NOT pinned with `#expectViolationAt` — the value is a dataset constant, so the anchor carries no information (the same reasoning as `CDISC-CG0308-violation-3-char-domain-LBX.cdt`)."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
---
S1 | LBX | 001 | 1
S1 | LBX | 001 | 2
---
